  "delivered": [
    "All six original public Petri-analysis functions accept an independent complete nine-field literal Petri net. Extended marking equations accept an ordered direct NativeString trace word, including empty words, duplicate/empty labels and arbitrary native bytes. Existing cached analysis workflows and CLI dispatch remain available.",
    "All twenty native option members across the 4/9/7-field structs retain exact defaults, supplied presence, signed markings, size_t budgets, NativeFloat64 vectors and both soundness variants. The existing cached soundness/Woflan panel exposes invariant_search_limit independently from max_states.",
    "Complete WorkflowMarkings, MarkingEquationResult, ExtendedMarkingEquationResult, WorkflowNetResult and SoundnessResult preserve all 2/14/13/9/52 fields, plus the actual bool helper result. Native entered/returned flags remain distinct from computed, feasibility, validity, status, exhaustion and result.error.",
    "The owned physical multipart envelope retains input/control/trace bytes, physical filename presence, part order and query origin. Before/after net, trace and selected options remain request-owned; canonical source/result/options/trace artifacts survive independently of optional legacy exporter failures.",
    "A standalone pre-mining Original Petri analysis workspace and adjacent cached-analysis launch expose complete tables, CSV, selected records, raw responses, reports, original requests and exact reusable artifacts. Native/API/portable/full frontend/strict build/live proofs are bound below; rendered browser behavior and every strict gate remain open."
  ],
